  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Watershed Management for Source Water Protection - NPI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  With FY 2022 fund this activity will:.Improve the availability of safe drinking water and gender-responsive sanitation facilities; The activity will strengthen long-term access to safe drinking water and reduce levels of water-borne disease by supporting community-based interventions on watershed governance and sanitation and protecting watershed sources through conserving forest and woodland ecosystems..Strengthen community and civil society organization engagement in the management of their natural resources and watersheds through increased engagement and technical assistance;.Develop opportunities for economically viable and sustainable livelihoods through the rehabilitation if WASH infrastructure; and.Work closely with communities to ensure that protected areas serve as anchor institutions that maintain critical ecosystem services.  .This activity will increase the water security and resilience of 137 communities, benefitting approximately 200,000 people and ecosystems that depend upon the Cross River Watershed in Cross River State and the Pai River Watershed in Bauchi State. Engaging a variety of stakeholders, this activity will rehabilitate dysfunctional WASH infrastructure, build new facilities, and develop support mechanisms for sustainability. This includes nature-based solutions, such as improved watershed management which have been underutilized yet have the potential to offer lasting, cost-effective improvements with multiple benefits for water resources, climate change adaptation, communities, ecosystems  and up and down stream community livelihoods. This activity links directly to JSP Goals 1 and 2, as well as Administration climate and water strategies..</narrative>
  </description>
